  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington delivered yesterday with strong retail momentum\u2014up 93% in a single day\u2014and add-on attach improved to 59%, the highest we've tracked recently. That's discipline from the front-of-house. Core grooming revenue dipped 8% day-over-day, but you had only 5 groomers working at $461 per groomer versus a trailing-30-day baseline of $514\u2014a capacity gap, not a performance issue. MTD you're running nearly flat to expectation (down just 1.4% after DOW adjustment), and year-to-date the store is up 49% in revenue on 51% more appointments. The one thing to watch: visit cadence is tightening in the positive direction, suggesting retention is improving\u2014keep that momentum.\n\nHicksville is your concern. Yesterday was a complete grooming shutout\u2014zero grooms, zero baths, zero add-ons\u2014which tanked daily revenue 78%. We need clarity on why no grooming happened and whether it was scheduled downtime or a staffing issue. MTD the store is actually performing 15% ahead of DOW-adjusted expectation, so this isn't a structural collapse, but the visit-cadence bucket is drifting the wrong way (growing from 10.2% to 12.6%), a leading indicator of stealth churn. You have $61.7k in annual value sitting in the lapse pool\u2014that's reactivation opportunity if we arrest the drift. Inventory across both locations is clean; no critical shortages.\n\n**Port Washington is staffed for 6 groomers today and 6 tomorrow with 7 bather hours; Hicksville is at 3 groomers both days with zero bather support; next 7 days Port has 34 groomer-days scheduled and Hicksville 15.**"
